    {
      "id": 8,
      "title": "Coverage and interpretation",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 36,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 6
      },
      "description": "",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Host:** exporter unavailable, sustained CPU pressure, low available RAM, low disk space, or read-only filesystems.\n\n**LLM:** exporter/API down, missing model, stale health or inference, repeated synthetic errors, and slow synthetic inference. Probe counters do not represent user API traffic.\n\n**GPU:** collection failure/staleness only in NVIDIA mode, high actual device temperature, and sustained VRAM pressure. CPU hosts do not fire missing-GPU alerts.\n\nRules are source-controlled in `roles/monitoring/files/grafana-alerts.yml`. Notifications remain muted by the separate policy; explicitly authorize and configure delivery before enabling it."
      }
